if you don't start a business around  something that you are intensely  passionate about you're going to fail  and most entrepreneurs get it wrong they  start a business just trying to make a  lot of money and they'll write into me  and say evan i want to make a lot of  money what business should i start and  that's the entirely wrong approach  the guys who started business just  trying to make money rarely do  if you look at any successful  entrepreneur at the core is always an  intense passion for what they're doing  and the desire to help people  starting a business is going to be one  of the most  grueling and cruel experiences you can  ever wish on somebody  you're going to get beaten down every  day people are going to say no they're  going to reject you they're going to  call you stupid  and you're going to question yourself  you're gonna wonder if this was a good  idea or not you're gonna wonder if you  should go back and just get a job you're  gonna wonder if you just made the  biggest mistake of your life  by starting this business  and the only thing that gets you through  the only thing that gets you through is  that intense passion for what you're  doing and knowing that you're helping  people  i remember when i first started helping  entrepreneurs i was asked to do a  presentation at the ymca  and i spent weeks preparing for this i  was excited to do it  and  we had a room full of chairs and i  remember walking into the building  full of excitement full of confidence  getting up the elevator walking into the  room and my heart sank  room full of chairs  weeks of promotion  three people showed up  and i wondered what's this what am i  doing what a waste of time  but the show must go on  and i delivered my presentation  it was awesome  and i helped those people that day i  touched them and i knew after that  presentation that i had to keep going  and doing this and i had no idea how it  was going to work out but i had to do it  even it was only three people at a time  this is what i was born to do and what  got me excited every day so i had to  keep doing it  and that's the scariest part  because quite often you have no idea how  the dots are going to connect but you  have to trust that somewhere in the  future  those dots will connect it will make  sense somewhere down the line and you  have to have the courage to keep going  forward even though  all you see around you is darkness  and that only comes  when you love what you're doing and you  know you're helping people  so if you're just starting a business  and you're thinking about different  ideas don't settle don't just try to  find something that's going to make you  a lot of money  you have to build a business around  something that you are intensely  passionate about and you know will help  a lot of people good luck
 

